On the positive side, he started with a magic marker and a
?oCharging. that should be very helpful if he survived the
early game! The sleep spell as a starter was quite helpful
throughout the game.

DL3 had a general store so price IDing made things easier.
DL3 also had the entrance to the mines. The first mine level
was lit so I poked about a bit, scored a pick ax and then
left for Sokoban. Food prayers were successful at 807, 2066
and 3550 with rations in between.

I was using daggers and occasionally throwing stars for
early thrown weapons but had an anxious moment when I met a
chickatrice up close as I rounded a corner. I ran. Later I
used sleep and thrown stuff to kill the chickatrice.

The Oracle was at DL8, kind of deep for this character.
There were two spellbooks but Zumwalt was too dumb for me to
try them.  Sokoban was finished easily enough, yielding a
(BoH at 6592. I tamed a horse with a lichen corpse just
before the zoo, it was a big help but didn't survive. I
believe it was in Sokoban where I found that wonderful =oSD!
Food, even with the vegan conduct was never much of an issue
after that.

DL10 was the big room so it was left for later. Back in the
mines, the second level was partially lit?! Bones? Yep.
Looking at the items I guessed the deceased was a wizard so
the opera cloak was probably a [CoMR. ML6 (the third mine
level) was minetown and it had an aligned altar! There were
5 very small shops, all 2x2 or 2x3 but I did get another MM
in the hardware store. One puzzling thing was a red naga in
a shop. That seemed a bit extreme for ML6 and it left a
corpse so it wasn't a chameleon and there shouldn't be a
poly trap this shallow.

On ML7 I lost the wielded weapon conduct at 9408 to a pick
ax accident but played the rest of the game without
intentionally hitting with a wielded weapon. There were some
more accidents but I never gained any advantage from them.

ML8 had the first poly trap and there was a cursed magic
lamp lying about. On ML9 I stepped onto a polymorph trap! 
"You feel a change coming over you. You shudder for a
moment",
whew. Then going back to Minetown to unburden, I hit a
second poly trap on this level and became a baby purple worm
losing my robe, the cursed cloak from the bones was a cloak
of MR but I couldn't cast any spells without my robe.

ML10 had 2 chameleons and a nymph with a /oCM making things
interesting. ML11 was the Mimic of the Mines ending and I
didn't have access to a spoiler at the moment. I thought I
had looked everywhere, even picking up a loadstone. I had a
possible (80z) ?oRC and got lucky when it was. Finally, when
I was about ready to give up, a nymph appeared and left a
ruby potion. I took a chance and it was object detection,
problem solved.

Back in minetown I finished all my BUC and price IDing and
looked like this when ready to head back to the main
dungeon:

