Usually once I finish the mines and Sokoban I feel pretty
good about things, but as a monk, I had no body armor and
this
martial arts stuff had me wondering. The next objectives
would normally be reflection and AC -15 but those looked
pretty tough still.

Back in the main dungeon I took on the big room. There was
much Elbereth-ing and running as appropriate but Zumwalt
prevailed, earning a pair of speedboots in the process! I
actually saw an elf put them on and speed up!

DL12 had a temple where I made my first donation. Then I
found the entrance to Ludious. I took out the denizens of
the first room by standing a knight's move from the door but
didn't feel ready to go further yet.

DL13 had a bones pile of an unfortunate wizard with the Eye
of the Aethiopica and Magicbane. The bones also yielded a
stethoscope, a unihorn and an unIDed amulet. Since there was
no BoH that rated to be an "oReflect! This was at bout
16,000 turns. I felt a lot more prepared but still pressed
further down before going back to Ludious.

DL15 held the portal to the quest. I poked around but was
eventually thrown out for lack of experience. DL18 had a
neutral altar I used when handy. My plan was to pray
immediately upon reconciliation for favors and spellbooks
but I was given Mojo at some point while checking to see if
my prayer timeout had expired.

DL19 had a poly trap where I engraved Elbereth and kept it
covered by a boulder when not in use. I transformed pets
here whenever I needed a shopkeeper or a priest bumped off.
My first effort changed my wolf (he was a dog but got polyed
somewhere in the mines without me noticing) to an iron
golem. There's a stout pet. He got swallowed by a trapper on
the next level!

DL23 put me over the top, it had a neutral temple and a
throne that yielded back to back wishes. I went for a [HoB
and a +oID. Strange but true! Now I was able to enchant some
armor that I expected to be a permanent part of my kit and
even started enchanting a stack of spears for throwing.

Next I went back and completed Ludious and returned to DL12
and then minetown to begin the multiple donation process. I
actually only donated the gold three times even though four
priests were available. I got into this role playing mood
and decided not to have the neutral priest on DL23 killed.
He even got mad at me once when I broke a /oCM while
standing beside him. By that time I had learned charm
monster so I calmed him. I got 13 points of protection from
donating.

Still wary of Master Kaen, I pressed on to the castle.
Medusa was no problem but I met a ki-rin just before the
castle that knocked me down to 60/133 HP. The castle was
easy, killed most of the moat creatures with thrown rocks,
froze the spot in front of the drawbridge, blasted the
drawbridge from a safe distance and went back into the maze
to fight the monsters one at a time from a position where no
ranged attacks could be used against me.

I found Sting, [GoP and more speed boots in the armory and
got a third throne wish which I used for a T-shirt. Finished
the VotD to see what was in the boxes, did some buffing and
polishing and set off to meet Master Kaen with a -33 AC.

I guess I was over prepared since Kaen presented no problem.
I hit him first with a !oPar but it affected me, too and I
didn't get many free shots at him. Then I fired off a sleep
spell and that did the trick. Later I wondered why that
worked since he had the Eyes of the Overworld, hmmm!

Now I set out for Gehennom. I had picked up a enough XLs
from incubi (yep, Zumwalt was a female by now) to get TC so
I did Gehennom from the bottom up. I levelported to the
bottom, cast magic mapping and sought out the VS. That was
marked with a light spell and up I went.

I would map the levels, dig out a path to the upstairs,
light that area and then, if large portions of the level
were unexplored, I would quaff a !oOD. I got a magic whistle
and a =oConflict this way. I had a terrible time with all
the usual demons, I just couldn't hit them hard enough. Most
ended up tormenting me until a cockatrice showed up and left
a corpse.

The shades were troublesome despite the fact I put on a
silver ring just for them. Then I discovered I had to take
off my gloves for the ring to work and that made me a
nervous wreck!

In Vlad's tower I found a jabberwock sleeping in a closet
and I tamed it with the charm monster spell and named it
Bandersnatch. I used up two /oSpeed to get Bandersnatch sped
up. He was a big help with the liches! He could put a lot
more damage on them before they teleported away than I
could.

Once I had finished everything except opening the wizard's
room, I went back and finished my preparations. I mixed up
34 !oEH (they were smoky) and got 170 HP and a =oFA. I fixed
all my armor and my spears and got my AC to -35. I took
along 11 c!oGL and about 25 ?oTeleport to speed my escape.
Of course with all this baggage, I was burdened but I would
use all this stuff on the way out, I've done it before.

At 44,438 I was ready to leave the castle to get the book. A
c?oTele got me started. When I was ready to open the room, I
dropped my bag in a safe place and stood diagonally from the
door on the ice to zap my /oDig, I've been dunked before by
the hellhound. Rodney went down to one shot from my /oDeath.
I grabbed the book at 44,803 and used the other c?oTele I
had out to get to the bottom. I did the ritual at 44,826 and
went down.

Crap, I forgot my bag! And I wasn't carrying much food!
Well, if things got desperate before I could recover my bag
I could return to the castle with the Eye and pack a lunch.
I recovered the bag and levelported back, this time to the
sanctum level, at 45020.

This is where things really got interesting! I didn't arrive
in the area on the right as I expected but on the far left!
A master lich was annoying me but I managed to light the
left side of Moloch's temple and the (BoO revealed the door.
Then the master lich summoned Demogorgon! I've spent hours
in some games trying to get a demon to summon Demogorgon but
I've never seen him outside of wizard mode.

And I wasn't too happy to see him just now! He made me ill
and I was burdened! I had visions of losing my first
character after the castle. I wanted to do two things as
quickly as possible, heal myself and get an Elbereth burned
into the floor. Since I could cast cure sickness and 0%
failure this should be a snap, except he had stunned me with
one of his other attacks. I know you can't cast spells while
confused and feared that the same might apply to stunned.

One course of action was to use the Eye to reach the castle
and then pray. Another was to dig in my bag for a !oFH. Both
scared me since I needed two turns and, being burdened, I
might lose a turn. Finally I decided to fall back on my
blessed unihorn even though each shot was only about 80% to
fix my problem. Lucky me, it worked.

Then Demogorgon seemed to lose interest in me. First he went
to Moloch's temple and later to the upstairs. I figured had
had killed the priest and and stolen the amulet and wouldn't
be messing with me any more. I decided to go make sure the
priest was dead, check out his spellbooks and then go after
Demogorgon. After Bandersnatch had killed the master lich
for me and I charmed some insects I made my way near the
door, used knock to open the door and jump to cross the fire
traps.

Imagine how foolish I felt when Demogorgon immediately
returned and sickened me. And I was still burdened! This
time he didn't stun me so a cure illness spell followed by
an Elbereth had the situation under control. Having screwed
up twice, I dumped the book, candelabrum, my pick ax, some
wands and five food rations and got out two !oFH and some HW
before I took another step. I hit Demogorgon and he left for
the stairs.

After checking the priests spellbooks I used a c!oGL to pop
upstairs. The plan was to use the stairs to drop in on
Demogorgon, slap down an Elbereth and beat him to death.
Just in case I decided to wear my "oLS instead of the "oR
for this encounter. Just as I took off my "oR and black
dragon came into range and fired off a disintegration blast.
It missed but the RNG sure was aggravating me.

So I popped the "oR back on and went down. I healed and put
down my Elbereth but Demogorgon had the stairs. Things just
weren't going according to plan. Next I tried to move him
with a /oTeleport but after 3 or 4 shots he hadn't budged. I
considered David Damerell's solution from his last YAAP. I
did have a /oWishing and a cockatrice corpse would clear
things up nicely. But I decided to do it my way.

I cast Cone of Cold at him several time and he never moved.
Then I hit him once and he went upstairs, I got out a
?oTeleport and followed and teleported to the upstairs
before he could. I briefly considered that I probably could
get him to carry the amulet back to the castle for me this
way and avoid any mysterious forces but rejected that plan
as too ambitious. I burned one more Elbereth as Demogorgon
came after me and then commenced to beat him to death. I got
this look with my stethoscope just before I finished him
off:

Status of Demogorgon (chaotic):  Level 50  HP 4(224)  AC -8,
scared, invisible.

That whole episode took 159 turns and it felt like forever.

